# Trivy vulnerability ignore list
# Format: CVE-YYYY-NNNNN [reason]

# CVE-2025-47273: setuptools — path traversal in PackageIndex.
# python:3.13-slim ships setuptools 70.3.0; the fix is 78.1.1. The production
# stage runs `pip install --upgrade "setuptools>=78.1.1"` but Trivy detects the
# version registered in the base image's pip metadata layer rather than the
# upgraded one. This application never invokes setuptools' PackageIndex at
# runtime — it processes PDF files only — so the path-traversal attack vector is
# unreachable. Re-evaluate when python:3.13-slim ships setuptools >= 78.1.1.
CVE-2025-47273

# CVE-2026-33845: libgnutls30t64 — GnuTLS DoS via DTLS zero-length fragment.
# No fixed version available in Debian 13 as of 2026-05-08; apt-get upgrade cannot
# resolve this. The application processes PDF files locally and never initiates or
# handles DTLS traffic, so this code path is unreachable at runtime.
# Re-evaluate when a Debian patch is released.
CVE-2026-33845

# CVE-2026-42496: perl-base / perl-archive-tar — path traversal when extracting
# tar archives. fix_deferred upstream; no Debian patch available as of 2026-07-30.
# This application never extracts tar archives — perl is an indirect OS dependency
# (poppler-utils) with no user-controlled archive extraction path.
# Re-evaluate when a Debian patch is released.
CVE-2026-42496

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964: msgpack — out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse after memoryview.
# msgpack is an indirect transitive dependency; this application never directly imports
# or calls msgpack's Unpacker class, so the vulnerable code path is unreachable.
# Trivy detects it from a Docker build layer that persists despite runtime upgrades
# due to BuildKit layer caching behaviour with cross-stage mounts.
# Remove when the package that pulls msgpack updates to >=1.2.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# Last review: 2026-11-03
# Next review: 2026-12-03
# Note: CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools) was originally removed thinking 3.13-slim would
# fix it, but python:3.13-slim still ships setuptools 70.3.0. Re-added with explanation.
# CVE-2026-97687/CVE-2026-97689 (urllib3) resolved by 3.13-slim migration (PR #282).
